\description{
A scheduled report is a standing subscription on one cluster: every
\code{interval_days}, \code{\link[=episodic_run_cron]{episodic_run_cron()}} emails the outbreak report -
the same self-contained HTML \code{\link[=episodic_report_render]{episodic_report_render()}} produces on
demand - to a list of addresses, as an attachment. It exists for
people who need to follow a cluster without an EpiSODIC account, or
with only a \code{viewer} one: a ward manager, a department head, a
referring physician. This is deliberately not the same thing as
\link{episodic_notifications}: those alert \emph{epidemiologists} that
something needs assessing; a scheduled report keeps \emph{everyone else}
informed once it is being watched, on a cadence they chose, without
needing to open the dashboard at all.
